{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-99627",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{7}$ from the denominator, all we need to do is multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{7}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{63}{4\\sqrt{7}} & = \\\\ \\frac{63}{4\\sqrt{7}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{7}} & = \\\\ \\frac{63\\sqrt{7}}{4\\cdot (\\sqrt{7})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{63\\sqrt{7}}{4\\cdot 7} & = \\\\ \\frac{9\\sqrt{7}}{4} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
